## Project in one paragraph

What it is, who uses it, what it is backed by, and the ONE quality bar that
should decide close calls (prototype vs. production, ship-fast vs. correctness).
An agent resolves a hundred small tradeoffs a day; this sentence is what it
resolves them against.

## Stack and versions

- **Runtime**: <language + version, and where it is pinned>
- **Framework**: <name + major version>
- **Data**: <database / ORM / client>
- **Tests**: <unit runner, e2e runner>
- **Tooling**: <formatter, linter, typechecker, dead-code>

Pin majors. An agent trained before your version will confidently use the old
API otherwise.

## Layout

| Dir | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `src/` | ... |
| `tests/` | ... |
| `.claude/` | Rules (auto-loaded), commands, hooks |

Note what is **absent** as well as present — a directory that was deleted, or a
pattern the repo deliberately does not use, is worth one line. Agents
reconstruct removed abstractions from memory.

## Setup

```bash
<the exact commands, in order, that take a fresh clone to a running app>
```

## Boot chain

`entry` -> `bootstrap` -> `providers` -> `routes`. One line each. This is what
lets an agent find where a global concern (auth, theme, error boundary) is
actually wired, instead of grepping for it.

## Commands

### Fast feedback (use these)

```bash
<single-file test>       # the targeted form, with any flag needed to avoid watch mode
<typecheck>
<format + lint fix>
```

### Everything else

```bash
<build> <full suite> <e2e> <coverage>
```

Mark which are slow and which are release gates.

## High-blast-radius actions (confirm before running)

<!-- Each row should also become a rule in .claude/guardrails.config.json, or it
     is documentation that nothing enforces. -->

| Action | Why it matters |
|--------|----------------|
| `<regenerate committed artifact>` | Overwrites a file the whole repo compiles against |
| `<write to remote database>` | No rollback |
| `<re-baseline snapshots>` | Silently erases evidence of a real regression |
| `<edit an applied migration>` | Diverges prod from the repo |
| `<push to the protected branch>` | Bypasses review |
| Editing generated dirs | Regenerate instead |

